      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:1yvi96n'
    '|b||Mine is colder. The guilt stays; the fine kills the fear instead. It tells you the worst that can happen is ten shekels.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7640
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:gpcupg'
    '|a||Either way, one brake goes, and twenty-five plus a ten-shekel price is thirty-five, under a forty-shekel temptation. So you come late.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 10240
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:g31zeb'
    '|b||And when the fine is dropped, nothing grows back. You can''t un-learn that the worst is mild, and a favour, once bought, stays a purchase.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 9480
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:1je78v7'
    '|a||Which means a big enough fine should still work. The textbook isn''t wrong; it just assumed nothing else changes.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7760
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:9ud9b6'
    '|a||In these made-up numbers, anything past fifteen, since one brake is still there; had both gone, it would take more than forty. For scale, a Haifa parking ticket then cost seventy-five shekels.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 11280
      voice: gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy
    '|b||So that''s when a price crowds out a norm: when the norm was doing the work, and the price is too small to take over.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7440
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:16814it'
    '|a||Want the parent''s sum in one line? Show the math, or skip it?':
      mp3: 
      ms: 4200
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:zdwvl3'
    '|a||A parent comes late when the worth of the minutes beats everything that holds them back.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6120
      voice: gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy
    '|a||Before the fine: forty is less than twenty-five plus twenty-five. On time.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 4960
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:10ew0y'
    '|a||With the fine, one brake gone: forty beats twenty-five plus ten. Late.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6200
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:qaja6'
    '|a||So to deter, the fine must top fifteen. If guilt and fear had both gone, it would have to top forty.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6960
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:1elmstd'
    '|b||A small fine turned a favour into a purchase. Do markets in general do that to us?':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6400
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow'
    '|a||Armin Falk and Nora Szech tested it in Bonn, with surplus lab mice that would otherwise be put down. Each mouse lived only if someone turned down money.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 10320
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:gzg7t9'
    '|b||Deciding alone, forty-six percent took ten euros and let their mouse die. Haggling in a market, seventy-two percent sold for ten euros or less.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 9360
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:8avaih'
    '|a||Their reading: in a market the guilt is shared. If I don''t sell, someone else will.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 5600
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:1watu'
    '|b||There''s an older view, though. In the 1700s Montesquieu argued that commerce makes manners gentler, because you have to deal fairly with strangers.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 8680
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:1m3x8ws'
    '|a||And there''s evidence for it too. Joseph Henrich''s team played sharing games in fifteen small societies, and the more of their food people bought in markets, the more fairly they treated a stranger.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 11080
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:rhz6h3'
    '|b||That''s a correlation, though. Markets might make people fair, or trade might spread where people already trust each other.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6720
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:1uk44zh'
    '|a||So how sure are we? That a price can crowd out a norm: mostly agreed, from about fifty experiments, which also find prices that strengthen norms.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 11320
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:triw2a'
    '|b||That markets make people worse, or better, overall: contested. A fine at a day-care centre is not a whole economy.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7400
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:nrlzgx'
    '|b||Three new cases. Harbourtown''s fishers keep the shared quay tidy out of habit and pride. The harbour council adds a $5 charge for nets left out overnight. What is the risk?':
      mp3: 
      ms: 12360
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:7xnkgl'
    '|b||More nets left out. A small charge can turn a courtesy into a cheap rental, and the pride that kept the quay tidy has nothing left to do.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 8960
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow'
    '|a||In a Swiss survey, about half of villagers said they would accept a nuclear-waste site nearby. Then each resident was offered a yearly cash payment for it. What happened to support?':
      mp3: 
      ms: 12600
      voice: gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy
    '|a||It fell, to about a quarter. Saying yes had been a civic duty; the cash made it look like a bribe.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 8160
      voice: gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy
    '|b||A town library charges a token 10-cent late fee, and many books come back late. It raises the fee to $5 a week. Going by the parent''s bar, what should happen?':
      mp3: 
      ms: 11360
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow'
    '|b||Fewer late returns: a fine too small to do the norm''s job backfires, but one big enough to clear the line still deters.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7440
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow'
    '|a||So do markets change people? Some prices do, because a price also tells you what kind of act you''re doing. Send the wrong message, and you keep paying for it, even after the price is gone.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 14240
      voice: gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy
    '|b||Pride kept the quay tidy, and a small charge turns that courtesy into a cheap rental: here, more nets left out.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7160
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow'
    '|b||The harbour council should hire you.':
